I've communicated that somebody from Posit made this message and, you know, sometimes you need to give access to personal data for whatever application you're doing, but oftentimes you don't.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:47.599
And by writing a custom MCP server, you own the code that does this so you can tailor it to whatever you need.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.479
So MCP or not MCP, that is a question.

00:15:51.559 --> 00:15:54.479
So MCP is, like I said, just an API standard.

00:15:54.479 --> 00:16:02.159
If you write your own and deploy it, you can really unlock a lot of capabilities for your agentic workflows.

